===Etymology 1===
[[File:Hangeul.svg|thumb|the word “hangul” in '''hangul'''|alt=한글 ㅎ=h ㅏ=a ㄴ=n ㄱ=g ㅡ=eu ㄹ=l]]
From {{bor|en|ko|한글|t=Korean script}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# The phonetic [[alphabet]] used to [[write]] the [[Korean]] [[language]].
#: {{syn|en|Chosongul}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The spelling {{m|en|hangul}} from the {{l|en|McCune-Reischauer}} transcription {{m|en|hangŭl}} is the more common English spelling, though {{m|en|hangeul}} (from the Korean spelling in the 1959-SK transcription and the 2000 South Korean Revised transcription) is sometimes preferred.
* {{m|ko|한글}} is the official name in South Korea, and {{m|ko|조선(朝鮮)글}} is the official name in North Korea; hence, scholars may prefer to use {{m|en|hangeul}} in reference to South Korea, and {{m|en|Chosongul}} in reference to North Korea.

